one `editable = \".\"` for the project itself), and there is no git, URL, path or directory source. CI sets `UV_FROZEN: 1` and every install is `uv sync --all-groups --frozen` / `uv run --frozen`, so the resolution cannot drift at build time and artefacts are hash-verified.","setup-uv's OWN CACHE (enable-cache: true) -- unlike the engine cache this one has no post-restore verification, so a poisoned entry would deliver arbitrary wheels into the venv. Rejected for the same scoping reason: a fork PR writes to an isolated cache scope, and writing to the default branch's scope requires push access, which is already full trust. No cross-boundary path exists.","destination.py's BROWSER SHIM AND SUBPROCESS -- src/adss/destination.py:_capture() builds a fixed argv list (no shell), and shim() derives its path component from `WANTED = re.compile(r'chromium(?:_headless_shell)?-(\\d+)')`, so group(1) is digits only and cannot traverse. The symlink targets come from a hardcoded /opt/pw-browsers glob, nothing is downloaded, and `adss shoot` is not invoked by either workflow.","EXTERNAL DATA RENDERED INTO THE MARIMO PAGE -- destinations/app.py interpolates warehouse-derived values into mo.md() f-strings, but only ints (total/months/countries, all wrapped in int() or n_unique()) and the min/max of order_month, a date-derived month key produced by the question's own SQL. Category values such as destination_country reach only Vega marks and mo.ui.table, which escape. Even granting a hostile OData response, there is no free-text field reaching the markdown renderer, and the page is a local developer artefact with no server. Not a supply-chain/CI concern and not concretely exploitable.","A DOC/TEST DISCREPANCY, NOTED NOT REPORTED: docs/adr/0004's Confirmation section claims 'tests/test_engine_pin.py asserts the binary's hash matches the committed .sha256', while that file's own docstring says the opposite ('The vendored binary itself is not hashed here'). The enforcement is real -- Engine.verify() at every invocation plus the CI `sha256sum -c` step -- so this is inaccurate documentation, not a missing control, and findings in docs and tests are out of scope."]}}
